\DOC DISCHARGE_MEMSAFE_TAC

\TYPE {DISCHARGE_MEMSAFE_TAC : tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Closes an existentially quantified goal asserting that the current event list
splits as a prefix appended to an earlier event list, with that prefix
satisfying a memory-access-inbounds condition.

\DESCRIBE
Takes no arguments. The assumptions {A} describe the machine state, the loaded
bytes, the event trace and the nonoverlapping/bounds side conditions, possibly
including an earlier {memaccess_inbounds} assumption for a prefix.
{
   A ?- ?x1. t = APPEND x1 u /\ memaccess_inbounds x1 ...
   =============================================================  DISCHARGE_MEMSAFE_TAC
}

\COMMENTS
In all observed traces, this is the only outcome, and it occurs only on goals
of this existential event-splitting and memory-safety form.

\ENDDOC
